I'm really pleased to welcome Michael Ford, the global marketing manager for Alpha Computers, who has flown in from California to give all of you an overview of the marketing campaign and to answer any questions you may have.

127
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:22,210
So please, give a warm welcome to Mr. Ford.

128
00:07:24,910 --> 00:07:25,710
Thank you, Jonathan.

129
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,670
It really is a pleasure to be here today.

130
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:35,390
It has been three years since I visited Beijing and it's clear to me that operations here are obviously going from strength to strength.

131
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:41,750
The Alpha brand continues to grow in leaps and bounds in China and that is certainly down to the hard work of all of you here.

132
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:44,030
So congratulations to all of you.

133
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:54,840
I'd like to start by outlining the key points of my presentation this afternoon and giving you an idea of the topics that will be discussed.

134
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:58,280
The presentation today is divided into five main parts.

135
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:07,800
First of all, I'd like to briefly touch on the background of the new X420 line, how the whole concept has come about and how the new product fits into our existing brand line.

136
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:11,760
Secondly, I'd like to present data on projected sales for the X420.

137
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,760
We will then go on to discuss our key rivals in this sector.

138
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:19,180
Then I'd like to go on to outline the campaign concept for the X420.

139
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:24,640
Finally, I'm happy to open up the discussion for any questions or points you may have for me.

140
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:32,080
All right, so we've prepared three phrases for you.

141
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:34,350
Let's take a look at those now on Fluency Builder.

142
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:36,810
Fluency Builder.

143
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:43,270
So this first phrase is really important because it's about the part of the speech that happens before the speech begins.

144
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:49,840
You know, usually you have a person who's going to talk about something, but you also have someone who introduces that person.

145
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,640
You know, this is John.

146
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,550
He's going to talk about computers.

147
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:53,770
He's very smart.

148
00:08:53,990 --> 00:08:55,050
Listen to everything he says.

149
00:08:55,470 --> 00:08:59,730
So we usually hear the phrase, let's give a warm welcome to.

150
00:09:00,070 --> 00:09:02,510
Yes, this is a very nice way of presenting someone.

151
00:09:02,610 --> 00:09:07,950
So obviously this person is talking to a group of people and he's introducing Mr. Ford.

152
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:11,550
So he says, let's give a warm welcome to Mr. Ford.

153
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:13,150
So that's saying let's clap.

154
00:09:13,410 --> 00:09:16,050
Let's say hello to him.

155
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:16,730
That's right.

156
00:09:16,910 --> 00:09:19,630
So like you said, this is an invitation to clap.

157
00:09:19,750 --> 00:09:21,090
You have to clap when you hear this.

158
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:24,170
Warm welcome means let's be nice to him.

159
00:09:24,270 --> 00:09:25,890
Let's all smile and encourage him.

160
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,920
You know, you think about it.

161
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:29,620
Someone who's going to give a speech is probably nervous.

162
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:31,540
And so this helps them feel comfortable.

163
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,100
That's right.

164
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:39,000
So it's a very nice way if you're maybe presenting someone who's going to talk, you can say, let's give a warm welcome to whoever you're presenting.

165
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:40,200
Okay.

166
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:45,580
Now when Mr. Ford was talking, he mentioned this very interesting phrase about operations.

167
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:52,040
He said, it's clear to me that operations here are obviously going from strength to strength.

168
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:52,440
Okay.

169
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,860
So that means things are going well.

170
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:56,450
You do one thing, you do it well.

171
00:09:56,770 --> 00:09:58,650
You move on to another thing, you do that well as well.

172
00:09:59,040 --> 00:09:59,310
Okay.

173
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,910
So that's what it means from strength to strength.

174
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,710
So we're saying that things are going from good to better.

175
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:05,310
That's right.

176
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:07,160
And getting better.

177
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:08,160
Okay.

178
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:09,160
And what about our last phrase?

179
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,530
Our last phrase is kind of similar to the last one.

180
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:14,650
The alpha brand continues to grow in leaps and bounds.

181
00:10:15,410 --> 00:10:15,830
All right.

182
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:18,070
So you can have a company that grows.

183
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,150
It grows a little.

184
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:21,610
You can have a company that grows quite a bit.

185
00:10:22,170 --> 00:10:24,750
Then you have a company that grows in leaps and bounds.

186
00:10:24,990 --> 00:10:26,010
That means a lot.

187
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,480
Okay.

188
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,970
So to leap is to jump, right?

189
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:30,470
That's right.

190
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:31,880
And so this is what we're saying.

191
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,600
We're just jumping higher and higher.

192
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,440
We're getting bigger and bigger or better and better.

193
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,020
That's right.

194
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:37,660
So this is an exaggeration.

195
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:40,620
It's like saying that it's not going quickly.

196
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:42,640
It's going the speed of light.

197
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,600
You know, it's just so fast.

198
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:45,800
All of a sudden, just really growing.

199
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,320
Okay.

200
